AB  - Effective fatigue monitoring during High-Intensity Interval Training is vital for athletic performance and injury prevention. This study introduces a non-invasive assessment framework based on DeepLabCut to extract biomechanical features from cycling videos. The proposed method quantifies physiological decay through core stability and upper-body compensatory movements. We incorporate physiological response lag theory by utilizing Heart Rate Recovery dynamics to derive the temporal parameter Lag. This parameter enables the construction of adaptive ground-truth labels to align visual features with metabolic states. Our FatiguePlusNet model combines 1D-CNN, Bidirectional LSTM, and attention mechanisms to capture complex spatio-temporal fatigue patterns. Experimental evaluations with professional athletes yield a mean Pearson correlation of 0.9401, with a peak of 0.9871. Ablation studies confirm that Lag. constraints and Bi-LSTM components are essential for modeling cumulative fatigue. This research provides a robust, contact-free solution for intelligent sports monitoring and training load management.  © 2026 Copyright held by the owner/author(s).
