TI  - A Fatigue-Aware Bicycle Type Recommendation for Cycle Tourism
PY  - 2025
T2  - GCCE 2025 - 2025 IEEE 14th Global Conference on Consumer Electronics
SP  - 521
EP  - 525
DO  - 10.1109/GCCE65946.2025.11275194
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105031453725?origin=resultslist
AB  - Cycle tourism is a growing global market; yet, novices often struggle to plan enjoyable rides, facing a mismatch between their bicycle choice, terrain difficulty, and personal fitness. To address this gap, we present a fatigue-aware bicycle route simulator. Our system integrates a physics-based speed model with rider-specific parameters and a Training Stress Score-based fatigue model to predict performance and automatically recommend rest points along any given GPX route. We evaluated the simulator in a factorial experiment comprising 54 scenarios across three real-world routes in Wakayama, Japan. The results demonstrate that rider ability is the primary determinant of performance. Moreover, our findings show that e-bikes significantly enhance accessibility, reducing travel time for tourists by up to 38% on challenging terrain. This work provides a practical decision-support tool that enables tourism stakeholders to optimize rental fleets and generate tailored itineraries, thereby better aligning their services with the diverse needs and abilities of visitors. © 2025 IEEE.
