AB  - Athletic is a very famous sport from school level to the international level. In this research, the investigators wanted to conduct the laboratory and field-based tests on athletes to know exactly about their body composition, physical abilities, and physiological variables to set and compare normative values and help them in improving the training strategies. Aim: To determine the physical characteristics, body composition, and physiological difference of middle- and long-distance runners and to compare physical, body composition, and physiological differences among national and state-level athletes. Design: A total of 41 (n = 41) sample size was taken from state and national level with the mean age of 24 ± 4. Cross-sectional study was carried out, the statistical analysis was based on descriptive statistics, and statistical analysis was done with the help of IBM SPSS Statistics 20 software. METHOD: Anthropometric measurements were carried out, to determine the body composition and physiological parameters among middle-distance and long-distance runners, the instruments used, namely, INBODY 770, CPET COSMED. Field tests like 12 min Cooper test were used. Result: There was no significant difference found in body composition and physiological variables except percentage of body fat, VO2 max, maximum heart rate, recovery heart, respectively. There was no such significant difference seen except VO2 max and maximum heart rate among state and national level long-distance runners. Conclusion: Body composition of middle- and long-distance runners is the same except percentage of body fat. VO2max of long-distance runners is high because of more hours of endurance practice. © The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Singapore Pte Ltd. 2025.
