AB  - The proceedings contain 45 papers. The special focus in this conference is on Statistics: Theory and Applications. The topics include: Quantile Functionals as Measures of Social, Health and Technical Events; The Unlikely Revolutionary: You, The Statistician — From ECT Confusion To AI Revolution: Discover How Statisticians Transformed Messy Medical Data into Life-Saving Insights; Leveraging Spatial Interpolation for PM2.5 Estimation: Constructing a Reference Framework for Calibration Models; physics-informed Gaussian Processes for Nonlinear Partial Differential Equations in a Fuid-Dynamics Application; physics-Informed Emulation of Systemic Blood Circulation; modelling of the Short-term Heart Rate Variability Measures: a Focus on the Transformation; pre, Peri, and Post-Covid Statistical Analysis of Restaurant Inspection Scores: Preliminary Insights; bayesian Network Modeling of Socio-Environmental Variables Supporting Health Policy Deliberation; bivariate Normal Distribution for Modelling Spatio-Temporal Data; Investigating Tabular Generative Models for Synthetic Data Generation in PDAC Bulk Gene Expression Data; poisson distribution: An Alternative Statistical Model to Predict Exact Scores of Football Matches; asymmetric Cross-correlation of Multivariate Spatial Stochastic Processes: A Primer; minimax Rates of Convergence for Multivariate Distribution Function L1Deconvolution with Known Ordinary Smooth Errors; assessing Ecosystem Dynamics under Disturbance: A Hidden Markov Model Framework for Species Detection Data; a Survival Analysis of Adolescent Dropout in Swimming; optimal Designs and Reliability Acceptance Sampling Plans for Accelerated Copula-Based Dependent Competing Risks Model; A Novel Optimised Fractional Hausdorff Grey Model with Time Power Term (OFHGM(1, 1, t훂))) for Forecasting Greenhouse Gas Emissions; performance Comparison of Statistical Emulators for Parameter Estimation in Complex Systems; circular-Circular Regression Models for Wind Directi