AB  - The Smart Truck Load Monitoring and Overload Prevention System with Ignition and Fuel Control is a comprehensive solution that tackles important issues facing the trucking sector. Truck transportation is essential for moving products over long distances in the modern global economy. Effective cargo load management does, however, provide several challenges, such as adhering to weight regulations, optimizing fuel use, and maintaining environmental sustainability. By creating an integrated system that combines cutting-edge sensor technologies, microcontroller systems, and communication networks, this research aims to address these issues. Load monitoring sensors, such as load cells and amplifiers, which precisely measure truck loads in real time, are at the heart of the system. As the system's brains, the NodeMCU-ESP8266 microcontroller processes load data and plan system actions. The seamless integration of mobile devices and onboard technologies enables fleet managers and truck operators to get real-time warnings and monitoring, resulting in improved safety, efficiency, and sustainability in transportation operations. © 2024 IEEE.
