AB  - Starting from the definition of training and the general rules that guide it, the effect of supercompensation is explained. Training is individualized through the quantification of the external and internal load and the analysis of the performance model. Training complexity depends on the athlete’s organism and its evolution during the development and maturity periods. Periodization has the objective of manipulate training load and recovery in order to achieve the best result at a specific moment. Strength plays a fundamental role in every human movement. Different strength expressions allow to modulate training and target it specifically for each athletic discipline. Nowadays, increased attention is dedicated to injury prevention, the use of sophisticated technology in order to control training load and recovery, and nutrition. Each track and field discipline (speed and hurdles, long-distance runs, jumps and throws) has particular characteristics, which are separately highlighted and discussed together with their main training components. © ISAKOS 2022, corrected publication 2022.
