AB  - The proceedings contain 74 papers. The special focus in this conference is on Human Aspects of Transportation. The topics include: Preliminary Experiment for Driver's Comfortable State Using EEG and HRV During Semi-autonomous Driving; Design and Implementation Content Validity Study: Development of an Instrument for Measuring Consumers’ Perception of Automatic Emergency Braking (AEB); keep Your Distance, Automated Vehicle! – Configuration of Automated Driving Behavior at an Urban Junction from a Cyclist’s Perspective; influence of the Relative Position of Surrounding Traffic on Drivers’ Take-Over Performance; user-Oriented Transport Solutions: An Ergonomic Investigation of Two Novel Concepts; poor Air Quality Along the Wasatch Front During Inversions: Role of Road Transportation and Possible Solutions; mind the Gap! Can Achieving Green and Efficient Rail Travel, with a Focus on Passenger Experience, Be Effectively Delivered Through Service-Based Contracts?; methods for Reducing the Complexity of Driving Workplaces in Commercial Vehicles; Passenger Expectation to Autonomous Bus HMI in Different Scenarios: A Field Study; smart City Transportation System in Developing Countries: The Case of Lusail City, Qatar; analysis of the Ergonomic Concept of Public Transportation in the City of Campinas (Brazil); still Unresolved After All These Years: Human-Technology Interaction in the Maritime Domain; task Oriented Use of Functionalities on Ship Navigation Systems; autonomous Ships: A Research Strategy for Human Factors Research in Autonomous Shipping; design of a Tool to Explore the Relationship Between Non-technical Skills and Resilience Capabilities; colour Design Method of Ship Centralized Control Cabin; construction of Crew Visual Behaviour Mechanism in Ship Centralized Control Cabin; preface.
