AB  - Wearable resistance (WR) provides the practitioner with the means to overload sprint running in a sprint-specific manner. this article investigates the effects of wr on sprint-running performance by discussing the mechanisms associated with WR, as well as those factors that must be taken into consideration by the practitioner when implementing a program that uses WR. In particular, the effects of different WR body placements (trunk, legs, and arms) will be discussed. practical applications and conclusions from the analysis will be provided. © 2019 National Strength and Conditioning Association.
