AB  - The proceedings contain 25 papers. The special focus in this conference is on ICT for Health Care, Embedded Systems for Biometric Data Acquisition, Biometric Data in Automotive, Home Applications, Biometric Data Analysis of Cardiac Signals and Gait Analysis. The topics include: The role of ICT in the Italian health care system; a non-intrusive model for the collection and analysis of data, feedback and needs; analyzing environmental conditions and vital signs to increase healthy living; preliminary study of a novel shelving system for nutrition habits measuring; a rule-based assistant system for managing the clothing cycle; state of charge monitor for wireless sensor networks; development of an algorithm and a sensor to monitor the heart rate by volumetric measurement techniques; piezoelectric energy harvesting on running shoes; implementing steganocryptography in scanner and angio-scanner medical images; stress-aware generation of recommendations in a driving system to increase user acceptance; stress map based information system for increasing road safety; an openCV based android application for drowsiness detection on mobile devices; distributed speech and speaker identification system for personalized domotic control; surface EMG fatigue analysis by means of homomorphic deconvolution; high performance dynamic threshold calibration for RR interval detection in a QRS complex using a parallel programing; an analog front-end for combined EMG/ECG wireless sensors; health monitoring in sport through wearable sensors; a new segmented-beat modulation algorithm for maternal ECG estimation from abdominal recordings and fall detection using wearable accelerometers and Smartphone.
