AB  - The proceedings contain 278 papers. The special focus in this conference is on Human Performance Development. The topics include: Nonlinear periodization from theory to practice; resistance training and functional capacity in physically frail older adults; the application of the yo-yo intermittent tests to elite soccer population; human thermoregulation and the cardiovascular system; neural and structural adaptations to electrical stimulation strength training; strength training for children and adolescents; new trends in high performance conditioning; traditional vs. cluster set configuration; efficacy of dry needling in elderly with nonspecific shoulder pain; improving quality of life and fitness in a woman with Parkinson's disease; arterial stiffness after an exercise program in patients suffering from chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD); evaluating long term functional outcome and fatigue related effects after anterior cruciate ligament reconstruction; relationship between different fitness tests and cognition in people with mild cognitive impairment; effects of using a cool vest in the neuromuscular function on specific soccer actions; sequencing training and performance in rhythmic gymnastics; criterion and concurrent validity of the 7 day-par in spanish adolescents; test-retest reliability of maximal 750M freestyle endless pool swimming; similar effects of two equated concurrent training programs; effect of running surface and fatigue state on impact acceleration in long-distance running; initial foot contact and centre of pressure during walking and running; impact of low to high intensity of resistance training program in enhancing leg strength among males; influence of lack of knowledge about the load in explosive parameters during bench press throws; the influence of augmented feedback and an external focus of attention on jump performance; effects of a 6-month resistance training on heart function and physical fitness in stable patients with chronic heart failure; effects of diafragamatic aspiration on physical and blood parameters of professional mountain bikers; analysis of the determining triple jump performance variables in competitions at different ages; effects of weighted vest on kinematics and kinetics during vertical; jump in soccer players; effects of compressive garments on the recovery from high intensity plyometrics; monitoring mechanical parameters during small sided games; effects of small-sided game training on vertical jump in football; basketball performance indicators during the ACB regular season from 2003 to 2013; high intensity interval training in patients with type 2 diabetes; increment of strength and muscular power in the school context; ACTN3 R577X polymorphism in marathon athletes; relationship between trunk stability and trunk muscular fitness; functional fitness and body composition in the Spanish elderly; sex differences in resistance training injuries during a weight loss program; hamstring extensibility of professional studies female dancers; effect of different warm-up intensities on swimming starts performances; conditioning priorities based on cricket batting shot frequency from the 2013 ICC champions trophy; unilateral vertical jump performance in soccer players; influence of three recovery methods on muscle fatigue and rate of perceived exertion; relationships between warm-up effects and swimming performances; nutrition status of Thai national team weightlifters; evaluation of the nutritional intake of soccer referees; aquatic plymetric training; functional fitness and health status in the Spanish elderly; influence of fatigue on lower limbs in landings with dominant foot; physiological responses during Valencian ball competition; rate of perceived exertion as a measure of cardiovascular stress; age difference on COP regularity in single leg quite stance; profile of two different methodologies for improve mechanical power; pre-competitive and competitive anxiety levels in hockey; lower limbs neuromuscular asymetries in female basketball players; neuromuscular basis of instability training with t-bow; heart rate recovery in elite beach volleyball male players; effect of high-frequency whole body vibration on lactate removal; acute and residual effect of vibration on hamstring flexibility; autonomic modulation in an ultraendurance mountain marathon; central nervous system fatigue after vo2max test in triathletes; pilates exercises in elite basketball; influence on outcomes of perceived exertion in soccer players; evolution of the record time among New York marathon master-runners and beach handball to improve jumping power.
