TI  - Express testing of anaerobic threshold and maximal oxygen consumption in skilled athletes
PY  - 2015
T2  - Teoriya i Praktika Fizicheskoy Kultury
VL  - 2015-January
IS  - 9
SP  - 73
EP  - 74
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84944038227?origin=resultslist
AB  - In the present paper the problem of improvement of testing system of athletes training load is considered. Sports practice proves the need of a daily assessment of adequacy of the training loads offered to athletes. Any data obtained in such daily researches are necessary for timely making some amendments in training process. The individual anaerobic threshold (IAT) is one of the most important physiological indicators of intensity of training load. The maximal oxygen consumption (V02max) is the main indicator of efficiency of cardiorespiratory system. V02max and IAT can be measured in a special laboratory. This procedure isn't always available to athletes and is a hindrance to trainings and competitions due to difficult organization. The researchers developed an express testing which can be used to detect the anaerobic threshold and the level of the maximum oxygen consumption without using expensive equipment and maximum physical activities. The running exercise - running the distance of 500 m on a racetrack of the stadium (or any other measured route) in 125-126 seconds with fixing of HR at the finish was offered as a load. Athletes could perform the offered exercise in the warm-up part of the training session. The developed express testing was checked experimentally in January-February, 2015. Two groups of athletes were involved in the experiment. The first group consisted of elite athletes: skiers, track and field athletes and orienteers. Athletes of mass categories were attributed to the second group. The statistical analysis of the interrelation of the test results obtained in vitro and during express testing showed a highly close relation (r = 0,8-0,9).
