AB  - Smart clothes containing small, noninvasive biosensors to acquire bio-signals like electrocardiographs (ECG), known as nanofiber technique-based wellness wear, are promising wearable computing devices for better healthcare, including obesity control, stress management, and chronic disease prevention and care. With the introduction of such a wellness wear system, this paper presents a software application involving a calorie tracker. The calorie tracker, running on an Androidbased smart phone, analyzes the ECG data obtained from wellness wear and provides a weight loss program using heart rate variability extracted from the ECG data. © 2011 NSP.
