UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/79952805585?origin=resultslist
AB  - Through making full use of the hydrokinetics and an aerodynamic model of a high-speed train named CRH3 in which contains three vehicles, the aerodynamic loads acting on the car bodies of the train with different speed were calculated with the software Star-CD/CCM + under the conditions of the cross wind with different velocities. Then the loads were dealt with as the external loads on the train in the dynamic model of the high-speed train including three cars. By dynamic simulation calculating with the software SIMPACK, parameters such as the coefficient of derailment, rate of wheel load reduction and factor of overturning were obtained, and influence of the cross winds on the dynamics of the high-speed train is simulated too. Results show that the influence of the first car of the train on the aerodynamic performance and running stability is greater than of the other cars when the train is running in cross wind. A non-linear relationship between the velocities of cross wind and the speeds of the train is discussed here. With reference to the safe operation criteria for high-speed trains, the maximum safe running velocity of the high-speed train under different-speed cross wind is specified.
