TI  - Acoustic emission and nonlinear elasticity in fatigue induced damage
PY  - 2005
T2  - 12th International Congress on Sound and Vibration 2005, ICSV 2005
VL  - 5
SP  - 3828
EP  - 3835
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84881568281?origin=resultslist
AB  - The internal structure of a medium affects its elastic properties and evidence has been found of the importance of the nonlinear elastic response to external loading in several materials, such as rocks, concrete, structural materials, ceramics and composites. The opposite is also true: perturbations inducing large amplitude mechanical waves (e.g. during fatigue cycling) modify the medium structure, leading to damage progression. Here, a model recently developed will be applied to study damage progression in SiC composites subject to cyclic loading at high strains. Acoustic emission events during loading/unloading and stress-strain cycles are analyzed.
