TI  - Neuroendocrinal and ortho-parasympathetic modifications during fatigue for the professional soccer team of Paris Saint-Germain (PSG)
ST  - Étude des manifestations neuroendocriniennes et ortho- parasympathiques de la fatigue dans le cadre du suivi biologique de l'athlète de haut niveau: Exemple chez les footballeurs professionnels du Paris Saint-Germain
PY  - 2005
T2  - Revue Francophone des Laboratoires
VL  - 2005
IS  - 375
SP  - 21
EP  - 27
DO  - 10.1016/S1773-035X(05)80149-2
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/29244466477?origin=resultslist
AB  - The scope of medicine in professional soccer is too often reduced to a traumatologic follow-up. The concept of fitness is often based to subjective parameters determined by coaches or physical preparer. When fatigue occurs, it is already too late, and sometimes the overtraining syndrom appears inducing dangerous consequences for the health of the athlete and fatal for his career. The longitudinal follow-up established by Sport Minister cannot unfortunately be the specific reflect of the state of form of a sportman during the course of the sporting season because it made only three time in the sporting season and the biological markers are not specific to the state of tiredness. Numerous works have shown that enhanced physical load could result in fatigue which is characterised by a decrease in physical and mental performance. Fatigue is caused by an energy imbalance between nutritional intake and energy expenditure due to muscular work. Supplementary chronobiological and psychological stress facilitates fatigue. The general effect of these different factors is responsible for hormonal and immune changes. The aim of our study was to determine within the scope of the longitudinal follow-up specific markers to the appearance of state of tiredness or overtraining. Thus, we have realized this experimentation on the professionnal soccer players of Paris Saint Germain Football Club for three seasons running. The main results show that a sporting season of a soccer player induces modifications of hypothalamo-pituitary and gonadal axis. The ratio testosterone/cortisol allows to appreciate the adaptation of the training load and during league match. The critical flicker frequency (CFF) analysis allows to evaluate vigilance state and central fatigue. © Elsevier SAS.
