AB  - Pain and discomfort in the legs are symptoms frequently encountered in elite athletes. In sporting disciplines where the athletes' posture is characterised by significant hip flexion (cycling, speed skating), 20% of such complaints are caused by flow limitations in the iliac arteries. Flexion of the hip induces excessive functional lengthening of the vessel which might result in kinking of the blood vessel, thereby impairing the blood flow. Endofibrosis, which is induced by increased hemodynamic stress on the vessel wall can further impair the blood stream. Non-invasive diagnostic tools (patients history, blood pressure differences) are the main diagnostic tools. Imaging techniques such as Doppler-Ultrasound and MR-Angiography are helpful in localising the lesions and planning therapy. Therapy options include the reduction of training load or operative techniques.
