AB  - Aim: Heart rate variability (HRV) indices of time and frequency domains of students before and after sport and teachers from different ages and health-state are analyzed with heart function information indicator. This article is designed to provide more scientific theoretical evidences for assessing autonomic pattern and systemic sub-health in healthy persons and patients by short-team HRV testing. Methods: Testees from Dalian University were enrolled from January 2003 to December 2005 totally 254 persons, including 142 male persons and 112 female persons, 175 healthy person-times aged from 20-39 years, 57 healthy person-times aged from 40-60 years, 100 student person-times of non-sub-health aged 20-25 years, fatigue after sport in 64 person-times, 40-60 years teaching staffs of sub-health was 22 person-times. MCA-3C heart function information indicator was used to analyze HRV for 512 times. Treadmill with 3 minutes fixed program 8-10 level running was performed till exhausted. All persons received HRV after 5-minute rest. The heart rate, (HR) which R-R interval minus average R-R interval was greater than 50 ms accounted for total HR percentage. T-S was total power spectrum. LF-S was power in low frequency. HF-S was power in high frequency. LF/HF was ratio between power in low frequency and power in high frequency. Results: 1 No significant difference was found in HRV of either sex and different ages. 2 The decrease of HRV was different in fatigue and sub-health status after exercise in undergraduate students. Conclusion: The results of examining HRV are reliable with heart function information indicator. It is suggested that HRV should be utilized as an index to assess people's health in national healthy exercise.
