AB  - Aim of this study was to evaluate whether use of Heart Period (HP) or Heart Rate (HR) may influence the spectral estimate of changes in Heart Rhythm Variability (HRV induced by physical exercise. For this purpose, power spectra were derivedfrom bothHP and HR signals monitored in 8 subjects before, during and aJer cycling. Powers around 0.1 (LF) and 0.3 (HF)Hz were computed, along with their ratio (LF/HF). Results indicate that HP and HR spectra provide different descriptions of HRV changes in response to exercise. LF and HF powers differed markedly whenever signijkant changes in the mean heart rhythm occurred, in some cases leading to opposite conclusions. A logarithmic transformationof HP and HR signals was proposed to obtain a univocal estimation of HRV spectra. © 1994 IEEE.
