AB  - Kaman Aerospace Corporation designed, developed and certified the K-1200 helicopter dubbed the 'K-MAX'. The helicopter was designed to be workhorse, an aerial track. In connection with this effort, a test was conducted to address the low cycle fatigue substantiation of the K-1200 drive system and airframe structure for the repetitive external load cycling and landing cycles derived from a high productivity logging mission. Overall, the testing demonstrated that critical components would not be compromised due to repetitive load cycling within prescribed replacement times.
