AB  - The work spindles of modern machine tools are often equipped with double row cylindrical roller bearings in combination with thrust ball bearings, angular contact ball bearings or cylindrical roller thrust bearings. The primary demand placed on the bearing arrangement is that it should provide adequate running accuracy. The stiffness in radial and axial directions is of considerable importance and can be maximised by choosing suitable spindle diameters, bearing preloads and distance between bearings as well as selecting the correct type of bearing. The article describes how the bearing arrangement is dimensioned with reference to the external loads, requisite bearing life and static safety. (A)
