AB  - A young athlete presents to the emergency room after a severe cycling accident. ECG-examination shows pathological findings. Abnormalities for cardiac rhythm, QRS-complex ST-segment and T-wave were found. The changes were benign and typical for the heart of endurance trained athletes, but differential diagnosis of these findings includes severe cardiac abnormalities. These ECG-changes are due to increased vagal tone, frequently encountered in athletes. They disappear with increasing heartrate.
