AB  - Sixteen distance runners were measured using resting heart rate (HR) resting heart rate variability (HRV) ranked running performance, and personality scales. The major hypothesis was that a low resting heart rate would be associated with high ranked running performance. There was no significant predictive relation found between HR and any of the measured variables, and performance was most related to age, intelligence and 'suppression'. HRV was associated with a group of personality measures.
